    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d661">

                <pb facs="0874" n="774" xml:id="pg774"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/83: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Ethiopia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">George</hi>)<anchor n="27" xml:id="d661-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-12-21T19:00:00-05:00">December 21, 1934—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. Your 27, December 19, 10 a.m. Please inform the Emperor that this Government
                    is confident that the unfortunate incident at Wal Wal, of which it has learned
                    with regret, is susceptible of settlement by peaceful means and that both of the
                    parties concerned will use their best endeavors to effect such a solution.
                    Explain that since the incident has been brought to the attention of the League
                    of Nations and since it is the intention of the Ethiopian Government to pursue
                    the matter before the Council, this Government considers that it could not
                    usefully or properly take any action. Assure the Emperor, however, that the
                    Department will continue to follow with sympathetic interest efforts made to
                    compose the dispute.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d661-f1" n="27" type="source" xml:id="d661-f1-content">
                <p>The substance of this telegram was communicated to the Consul at Geneva and to
                    the Ambassador in Italy as Department’s No. 131 and No. 108, respectively,
                    December 21, 7 p.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
